  {
   "id": "textbook",
   "scene": "textbook",
   "text": "Now for the textbook link! In Primary Six, you learn about decomposers. Bacteria and fungi break down dead plants and animals into simpler substances. These go back into the soil, and plants use them to grow. Without decomposers, dead things would pile up, and the soil would run out of nutrients.",
